abstract: >-
  A free, sector-neutral method for deciding, on evidence, whether a deployed
  AI system or AI agent should keep operating, be restricted, or be stopped,
  adapted from aviation safety management. A two-question test rates each
  capability of a system; five operational control states cover both the model
  and the service around it; 36 requirements in seven domains scale with
  consequence (8 apply to low-consequence systems); and fixed rules turn
  findings into Ready, Ready with Conditions or Not Ready per capability,
  without a numeric score. Includes templates, worked examples including an AI
  agent, a mapping to ISO/IEC 42001, the NIST AI RMF and the EU AI Act, an
  assessment workbook, a machine-readable rules file and an AI assistant skill.
keywords:
